Here are the step-by-step instructions to install Node.js on both Linux and Windows:

=>Installing Node.js on Linux

1. Open Terminal: Press `Ctrl + Alt + T` to open the terminal.

2. Update Package Index: Run the following command to update your package index:

   bash
   -----------------------
   sudo apt update
   -----------------------
   


3. Install Node.js: Use the following command to install Node.js:
   bash
   ---------------------------
   sudo apt install nodejs
   ---------------------------
   
4. Install npm: Install npm (Node Package Manager) with:
   bash
   -----------------------
   sudo apt install npm
   -----------------------
   
5. Verify Installation: Check the installed versions of Node.js and npm:
   bash
   -----------------------
   node -v
   npm -v
   -----------------------

=>Installing Node.js on Windows

1. Download Installer: Go to the [official Node.js website](https://nodejs.org) and download the Windows installer (LTS version is recommended).

2. Run Installer: Double-click the downloaded `.msi` file to start the installation.

3. Follow Setup Wizard:
   -> Click "Next" on the welcome screen.
   -> Accept the license agreement and click "Next".
   -> Choose the installation directory and click "Next".
   -> Select the components you want to install and click "Next".
   -> Click "Install" to begin the installation.
   
   
4. Complete Installation: Once the installation is complete, click "Finish".

5. Verify Installation: Open Command Prompt and check the installed versions:
   
   ->cmd
   -----------------------
   node -v
   npm -v
   ----------------------
   


